Multiply both sides by \(k/4.5\):

\[
- x = x - 9 \implies - x - x = -9 \implies -2x = -9 \implies x = \frac{9}{2} = 4.5.
\]

Find \(y\):

\[
y = -\frac{4.5}{k} \cdot 4.5 = -\frac{20.25}{k}.
\]

Recall \(k = \frac{33}{4 \sqrt{14}}\):

\[
y = -\frac{20.25}{\frac{33}{4 \sqrt{14}}} = -20.25 \cdot \frac{4 \sqrt{14}}{33} = -\frac{81}{4} \cdot \frac{4 \sqrt{14}}{33} = -\frac{81 \cdot 4 \sqrt{14}}{4 \cdot 33} = -\frac{81 \sqrt{14}}{33} = -\frac{27 \sqrt{14}}{11}.
