- When \(|t| \in [0,0.5]\),
\[
f(t) = 0.5 - |t|.
\]
- When \(|t| \in [0.5,1]\),
\[
f(t) = |t| - 0.5.
\]

Thus:
\[
f(t) = 
\begin{cases}
0.5 - |t|, & |t| \leq 0.5, \\
|t| - 0.5, & |t| \geq 0.5.
\end{cases}
\]

