\[
N_1 = 1000 \times 1 + 100B + 10C + D = 1000 + 100B + 10C + D \equiv 0 \pmod{7}
\]
\[
N_2 = 1000 A + 100 \times 1 + 10 C + D = 1000A + 100 + 10C + D \equiv 0 \pmod{7}
\]
\[
N_3 = 1000 A + 100 B + 10 \times 1 + D = 1000A + 100B + 10 + D \equiv 0 \pmod{7}
\]
\[
N_4 = 1000 A + 100 B + 10 C + 1 = N - D + 1 \equiv 0 \pmod{7}
\]

Rewrite \( N = 1000A + 100B + 10C + D \).

---

**Step 3: Express these conditions using \( N \)**

1. For \( N_1 \):
\[
1000 + 100B + 10C + D \equiv 0 \pmod{7}.
\]
Note that:
\[
N = 1000 A + 100B + 10C + D,
\]
so
\[
N - 1000(A-1) = 1000 + 100B + 10C + D \equiv 0 \pmod{7}.
\]
Therefore,
\[
N \equiv 1000(A -1) \pmod{7}.
\]

2. For \( N_2 \):
\[
1000 A + 100 + 10 C + D \equiv 0 \pmod{7}.
\]
Compare to \( N \),
\[
N - 100(B -1) = 1000A + 100 + 10C + D \equiv 0 \pmod{7}.
\]
So,
\[
N \equiv 100(B -1) \pmod{7}.
