Here, 120° because \(BA\) points at 180° from x-axis, and the angle is \(60^\circ\) between \( BA \) and \( BC \). So \( BC \) is at 120° from x-axis.

Calculate \( C \):

\[
C = B + BC = (14,0) + (-3.5, 7\sqrt{3}/2) = (10.5, 7\sqrt{3}/2)
